        {
            "name": "Get Specific Scan",
            "event": [
                {
                    "listen": "test",
                    "script": {
                        "exec": [""],
                        "type": "text/javascript",
                        "packages": {},
                        "requests": {}
                    }
                }
            ],
            "request": {
                "method": "GET",
                "header": [],
                "url": {
                    "raw": "{{base_url}}/scans/:filename",
                    "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
                    "path": ["scans", ":filename"],
                    "variable": [
                        {
                            "key": "filename",
                            "value": "sample_output.json",
                            "description": "The filename of the scan result to retrieve. Must be a valid JSON file from the scans list."
                        }
                    ]
                },
                "description": "Retrieve a specific enumeration scan result by filename.\n\n**Endpoint:** `GET /scans/:filename`\n\n**Path Parameters:**\n- `filename`: The JSON filename of the scan result (e.g., `example.com_20260101_120000.json`)\n\n**Description:**\nReturns the complete enumeration result for a previously saved scan. This includes all subdomain information, validation results, and metadata.\n\n**Response Structure:**\nReturns the full `EnumerationResult` object:\n- `domain`: The enumerated domain\n- `timestamp`: When the enumeration was performed\n- `total_subdomains`: Total discovered subdomains\n- `active_subdomains`: Number of active subdomains\n- `subdomains`: Complete list of all subdomains with details\n- `active`: List of active subdomains\n- `inactive`: List of inactive subdomains\n- `whois_info`: WHOIS information (if available)\n\n**Status Codes:**\n- `200 OK`: Successfully retrieved scan result\n- `400 Bad Request`: Invalid filename (contains path traversal characters)\n- `404 Not Found`: Scan file does not exist\n- `500 Internal Server Error`: Failed to read scan file\n\n**Security:**\nThe endpoint prevents directory traversal attacks by validating the filename.\n\n**Use Cases:**\n- Retrieve detailed results from previous enumerations\n- Compare results across different time periods\n- Export data for further analysis"
            },
            "response": [
                {
                    "name": "Success",
                    "originalRequest": {
